hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1504","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawrqi and Salam bin Junada told us, they said: Abu Muawiyah told us, Al-Dawrqi said: Al-A’mash told us, Salam said: On the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you performs ablution and then comes to the mosque, He is only motivated by prayer, he only wants to pray, so when he enters the mosque he is in prayer, prayer is not what would detain him, and the angels send blessings upon any of you. As long as he is in the seat in which he prayed, they say: O God, forgive him, O God, have mercy on him, O God, accept his repentance as long as he did not harm him, unless he did it. \in it\"""""""
